* Central Gravity Inward Pull
* How it works: Form a closed boundary loop of standard physics particles. Instead of changing joint lengths, apply a continuous inward force vector to each boundary particle directed toward the geometric center of the disks.
   * Shrinkage: The force acts like a tight rubber band snapping shut.
   * Pros: Highly stable and self-correcting.
   * Cons: Can get snagged easily on protruding disks, preventing optimal tight packing in deep pockets.
