## 2. Geometric & Computational Geometry Algorithms (Static Approaches)
If you do not need active animations and just want the final, mathematically perfect tightest fit, purely geometric algorithms are faster, lighter, and completely stable.

* Taut String / Convex Hull Wrapping
* How it works: Treat the disks as physical obstacles. Treat the blob boundary as a geometric path. Utilize an altered Gift Wrapping (Jarvis March) algorithm where line segments must sit perfectly tangent to the exterior edges of the disks.
   * Shrinkage: Mathematically calculates the shortest path bounding a set of circles.
